From 3120da92d5c260f568514e593b8e6f66be3bdb21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 09:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move NET PLAY to the top row, and give the panel a door

The button was in the bottom-right slot next to LOAD and EXIT, which is
the wrong home for the only route into the panel and crowded besides. It
now sits in the gap on the top row between the map size and the dice -
the one 32-wide slot free on every screen, since MISSION keeps its arrows
at x 284 and CUSTOM its dice at 220. NETPLAY_BTN_X and NETPLAY_BTN_Y move
it.

It is a toggle now. That matters more than it sounds: EXIT quits the
game, so with a one-way button the panel was a room with no door. The
same press goes back to whichever screen it was opened from.

ADD AN ADDRESS gets its own row under the list. It was sharing the
bottom-right slot with the LOAD icon, which is still drawn there - a
button that reads LOAD and adds an address is worse than no button. LOAD
is not drawn on this screen at all now, since it does nothing here, and
the list is eight rows so it stops above the ADD row rather than running
under it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFktm5o1kLnS2Pgvyp8tD4
---
 scripts/scr_game_init/scr_game_init.gml | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/scr_game_init/scr_game_init.gml b/scripts/scr_game_init/scr_game_init.gml
index 25676fd6..c782dca3 100644
--- a/scripts/scr_game_init/scr_game_init.gml
+++ b/scripts/scr_game_init/scr_game_init.gml
